{"to": "8684633270", "subject": "Method 006: Negative Harmony / Polarity Inversion", "body": "🎵 *Methods DB Update — Method 006 Added*\n\n*Method:* Negative Harmony / Harmonic Polarity Inversion\n*Type:* Traditional-Theoretical / Neo-Riemannian (AI-Compatible)\n*Source:* Ernst Levy, *A Theory of Harmony* (1985); Steve Coleman (coiner); Jacob Collier (popularizer)\n\n*Core Idea:*\nEvery pitch/chord has a \"negative\" counterpart — reflect across tonic-dominant axis (C↔G in C major). Major↔minor swap. Ascending↔descending inversion. Functional gravity preserved — negative chord pulls toward negative tonic with same strength as original.\n\n*UnitMatrix Impact:*\nEach cell stores (original_material, negative_material, axis). Voices/Sections toggle polarity independently. Horizontal alternation (Orig→Neg→Orig) or vertical mirror counterpoint (Voice 1 original, Voice 2 negative).\n\n*Element Coverage:*\n- PITCH: neg(pitch) = axis - pitch — melodic contour inverted\n- RHYTHM: Pattern preserved; accent emphasis flips (strong→off-beat)\n- HARMONY: G7→D♭maj7 (tritone sub); Dim7 symmetrical; HOME/TENSE labels map across axis\n- STRUCTURE: Section toggleable Orig/Neg/Hybrid; tension arcs invert\n- TEXTURE: Arpeggiation direction flips; register spreads mirror\n\n*Key Artists:* Jacob Collier (In My Life reharm), Steve Coleman / M-BASE, Ernst Levy\n\n*Controllability:* Axis placement (tonic-dominant or custom). Per-voice polarity toggle. Per-Section alternation. Hybrid partial reflection. Cascade: reflect PITCH → derive HARMONY → adjust TEXTURE.\n\nSee: /opt/data/projects/Research/CompositionMethods/methods_db.md"}